  => single runs are scale-equivalent to consecutive AP: CONFIRMED

CONSEQUENCE (rigorous): a SINGLE full arithmetic run, at ANY spread, has
mu = a(k) EXACTLY (L1 scale-invariance).  So a spread bound is needed ONLY
for MULTI-BLOCK or PERFORATED shapes.  Single-run shapes never undercut a(k).

